WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.152
A vital sign is useful when you know what it measures and how it was obtained. A displayed value with an unknown unit, poor signal or wrong cuff is not yet trustworthy clinical information.
只有知道测量对象及取得方式，生命体征才有用。单位不明、信号不佳或袖带错误的显示值，还不能算可靠临床信息。

00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:24.528
Typical adult reference ranges help you notice a departure from expectation. They are not diagnoses, universal treatment targets or proof of safety when a value lies inside them.
常用成人参考范围帮助发现偏离预期，但它们不是诊断、统一治疗目标，也不保证范围内就安全。

00:00:24.528 --> 00:00:34.944
Every measurement belongs to a time, method and context. Record whether oxygen was being given, whether the patient had moved and whether a treatment had just occurred.
每个测量都属于某个时间、方法及背景。记录当时是否吸氧、是否刚搬动，以及是否刚接受治疗。

00:00:34.944 --> 00:00:45.696
Your assessment begins before the monitor is attached. Immediate threats are managed while reliable measurements are obtained, not after every device finishes cycling.
评估在连接监护仪前已经开始。获得可靠测量时就应处理即时威胁，不必等每个设备都完成测量。

00:00:45.696 --> 00:00:58.872
Brain function depends on oxygen, glucose and perfusion. New confusion can therefore be a neurological problem, but also a sign of a respiratory, circulatory or metabolic emergency.
脑功能依赖氧、葡萄糖及灌注。因此新发混乱可能是神经问题，也可能提示呼吸、循环或代谢急症。

00:00:58.872 --> 00:01:09.264
Blood pressure is a pressure measurement, not a direct measurement of blood flow to every organ. Skin and mentation provide additional evidence about perfusion.
血压测的是压力，不直接测每个器官血流。皮肤和意识提供额外灌注证据。

00:01:09.264 --> 00:01:23.088
Saturation estimates oxygen loading of hemoglobin. Respiratory observation and capnography address different questions about ventilation and carbon dioxide; none can safely stand in for all the others.
血氧饱和度估计血红蛋白携氧比例。呼吸观察及呼气二氧化碳监测回答通气与二氧化碳的不同问题；它们不能彼此完全替代。

00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:33.000
An ECG describes electrical activity. A coherent tracing can coexist with no effective pulse, so always correlate the screen with the patient.
心电图描述电活动。看似有组织的波形可以与无有效脉搏并存，因此屏幕始终要与患者实际情况相对照。

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Record the value the instrument or your observation actually supports. Do not round every respiratory rate to twenty or write one hundred and twenty over eighty because the patient looks well.
记录仪器或实际观察所支持的数值。不要把每次呼吸频率都凑成二十，也不要因为看起来良好就写一百二十比八十。

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:58.344
A manual instrument has limited graduations. Use its actual resolution rather than adding a decimal place that was never measured. A digital value should retain the displayed precision appropriate to the device.
手动仪器刻度有分辨率限制，应按真实分辨率记录，不要添加未测得的小数。数字仪器按其适当显示精度记录。

00:01:58.344 --> 00:02:10.776
Include time, method, site and clinically relevant conditions. A saturation without oxygen device and flow, or a temperature without route, can be difficult to compare later.
记录时间、方法、部位及临床相关条件。血氧没有给氧装置和流量，或体温没有途径，后续可能无法合理比较。

00:02:10.776 --> 00:02:22.824
If a value cannot be obtained, document why and continue assessment and care. Missing information is a problem to manage, not permission to manufacture a normal result.
无法获得某值时，说明原因，并继续评估照护。缺失信息需要处理，但不能编造正常值。

00:02:22.824 --> 00:02:35.040
Start by checking factors that interfere with a response. Observe eye opening and speech before adding a stimulus; use a clear spoken request before a trained pressure stimulus is considered.
先检查影响反应的因素。加刺激前观察睁眼及言语；先清楚口头指令，必要时才考虑受训的压力刺激。

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:49.248
Eye opening scores four spontaneously, three to sound, two to pressure and one when absent without a limiting factor. Swollen-shut eyes are not automatically evidence of the lowest neurological response.
睁眼自发四分、声音三分、压力两分，在无限制因素时完全不睁眼一分。因肿胀闭眼，不能自动视为最低神经反应。

00:02:49.248 --> 00:03:01.032
Verbal response scores five for orientation, four for confused but coherent communication, three for intelligible words, two for sounds and one for none when assessable.
言语定向正常五分，意识混乱但连贯交流四分，可辨单词三分，声音两分，可评估但完全无言语一分。

00:03:01.032 --> 00:03:14.928
A language barrier, intubation or another limiting factor may make a component not testable. Record the component and reason instead of treating an inability to speak as a neurological score of one.
语言障碍、插管或其他限制可能使某项不可测。应记录该分项及原因，不能把无法说话直接当作神经性一分。

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:27.264
Motor response scores six for obeying commands and five for purposeful localization. Localization is not merely moving a limb away; it is a directed response toward the stimulus.
运动遵嘱六分，有目的定位五分。定位不只是肢体退开，而是朝向刺激的定向反应。

00:03:27.264 --> 00:03:39.288
Normal flexion or withdrawal scores four. Abnormal stereotyped flexion scores three, extension two, and no response one when the response can genuinely be tested.
正常屈曲或回缩四分，异常刻板屈曲三分，伸展两分，在确实可测时完全无反应一分。

00:03:39.288 --> 00:03:49.824
Use the highest observed response for the component, but also document a meaningful difference between sides. The best-side score must not conceal a focal deficit.
分项采用观察到的最佳反应，但也应记录重要左右差异。最佳侧评分不能隐藏局灶缺损。

00:03:49.824 --> 00:04:19.176
Use the check, observe, stimulate and rate sequence. The structured aid names fingertip pressure, trapezius pinch and supraorbital-notch pressure. Selection and interpretation require supervised training; avoid the injured area, pressure on the eyeball, sternal rubbing and repeated unnecessary stimulation. Finger pressure is peripheral, not a central stimulus. Do not practise painful stimuli on peers.
使用检查干扰、观察、刺激、评分的顺序。结构化辅助表列出指尖压力、斜方肌捏压及眶上切迹压力。选择及判读需要督导训练；避开受伤区域，不压眼球，不做胸骨摩擦，也不反复施加无必要刺激。指端压力是外周刺激，不是中央刺激。不要在同伴身上练习疼痛刺激。

00:04:19.176 --> 00:04:31.968
In this original example, eyes open to sound, conversation is confused and commands are obeyed. The components are E three, V four and M six, giving thirteen.
原创例中，声音引起睁眼、交谈混乱、能够遵嘱，分项为 E3、V4、M6，总分十三。

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:45.048
Six minutes later, eyes open only to pressure, verbal output is single words and the best motor response localizes. E two, V three and M five total ten.
六分钟后，只对压力睁眼、言语为单词、最佳运动为定位。E2、V3、M5，总分十。

00:04:45.048 --> 00:04:56.376
The decline is clinically important. Reassess airway, ventilation, perfusion, glucose and the relevant cause rather than waiting for a total of eight before becoming concerned.
下降具有临床意义。应复评气道、通气、灌注、血糖及相关原因，而不是等总分降到八才担忧。

00:04:56.376 --> 00:05:09.240
A low score describes responsiveness; it does not identify the diagnosis. Brain-injury severity bands apply in the appropriate trauma context, not to every patient with the same total.
低分描述反应程度，不能识别诊断。脑损伤严重度分档适用于适当创伤背景，不适用于所有总分相同的患者。

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:20.880
Explain the assessment and choose a site appropriate to age and condition. Use finger pads over the artery and adjust gentle pressure until you can clearly feel pulsations.
解释评估，按年龄及情况选择部位。用指腹接触动脉，调整轻柔压力，直至明确触到搏动。

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:33.336
Count with a clock, not by estimation. A regular pulse can be counted over an approved shorter interval and converted; irregularity needs a longer count, usually a full minute.
使用时钟计数，不凭感觉估计。规律脉搏可按获准较短时间计数再换算；不规则时需要更长计数，通常完整一分钟。

00:05:33.336 --> 00:05:45.576
Describe rhythm and amplitude in addition to rate. If the monitor and palpable pulse disagree, check the patient, signal and possible pulse deficit rather than choosing the more reassuring number.
除频率外还描述节律和幅度。监护心率与触诊脉搏不一致，应检查患者、信号及可能的脉搏短绌，不能只选更安心的数字。

00:05:45.576 --> 00:05:56.280
Do not let a prolonged routine pulse count delay arrest recognition. An unresponsive patient is assessed using the appropriate rapid breathing-and-circulation pathway.
不要因长时间例行数脉而延误骤停识别。无反应患者应按适当快速呼吸循环流程评估。

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:08.616
Sixty to one hundred beats per minute is a common resting adult reference. Fever, pain, anxiety, hypovolemia, medication and rhythm disturbances can change the rate.
每分钟六十到一百次是常用成人静息参考。发热、疼痛、焦虑、低血容量、药物及心律失常均会改变心率。

00:06:08.616 --> 00:06:21.912
A slow rate may be normal for a particular person or may accompany serious disease. Determine whether the patient has poor perfusion, chest discomfort, altered mentation or other concerning findings.
某人的慢心率可能是常态，也可能伴严重疾病。应判断是否有灌注不良、胸部不适、意识改变或其他担忧发现。

00:06:21.912 --> 00:06:32.424
A rapid pulse with normal blood pressure can be a compensatory warning rather than reassurance. Compare serial rate, skin, mentation and breathing.
脉快但血压正常可能是代偿警示，而不是安心依据。应连续比较心率、皮肤、意识及呼吸。

00:06:32.424 --> 00:06:43.896
A radial pulse is not a blood-pressure gauge and does not prove adequate cerebral perfusion. Never substitute the old pulse-location pressure rule for measurement and assessment.
桡动脉不是血压计，也不证明脑灌注足够。不能以旧的脉搏部位估血压规则，代替测量和评估。

00:06:43.896 --> 00:06:54.600
Watch actual chest or abdominal movement. Count one complete respiratory cycle as one breath, with a timed observation long enough to represent the pattern.
观察真实胸或腹运动，一个完整呼吸周期算一次，计时观察应足以代表其模式。

00:06:54.600 --> 00:07:07.296
For a regular adult pattern, thirty seconds may be appropriate; irregular breathing and infant periodic patterns require a full minute. Do not quietly assign eighteen to every patient.
成人规律呼吸可用三十秒；不规则及婴儿周期性呼吸需要完整一分钟。不要默认每位患者都是十八次。

00:07:07.296 --> 00:07:20.088
Note depth and work of breathing, including accessory muscles, retractions, nasal flaring, paradoxical motion and speech limitation. A rate alone misses how effective each breath is.
记录深度及呼吸功，包括辅助肌、凹陷、鼻翼扇动、矛盾运动及言语受限。频率本身无法体现每次呼吸的有效性。

00:07:20.088 --> 00:07:30.816
Children often breathe faster and show abdominal movement more prominently. Adult reference limits must not be applied as if they were normal pediatric ranges.
儿童通常呼吸更快，腹部运动更明显。成人参考界限不能直接当作儿童正常范围。

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:43.704
Tachypnea describes a fast rate, commonly above twenty in adults; bradypnea describes a slow rate, commonly below twelve. Neither label alone tells you whether ventilation is adequate.
呼吸过速描述频率快，成人常以超过二十次界定；呼吸过缓描述频率慢，常以低于十二次界定。名称本身不说明通气是否足够。

00:07:43.704 --> 00:07:56.496
Kussmaul breathing is deep compensatory ventilation associated with metabolic acidosis, such as diabetic ketoacidosis. Do not automatically coach it slower as though it were anxiety.
Kussmaul 呼吸是代谢性酸中毒相关的深大代偿通气，例如糖尿病酮症酸中毒。不能自动当作焦虑而指导减慢。

00:07:56.496 --> 00:08:11.064
A waxing-and-waning pattern with apnea is described as Cheyne-Stokes. Irregular grouped breaths and unpredictable apnea may be described as Biot-type or ataxic breathing; examine the patient rather than relying on a label.
伴暂停的渐强渐弱模式称 Cheyne-Stokes。成组不规则呼吸及不可预测暂停可描述为 Biot 型或共济失调性呼吸；重点是检查患者，而非只给名称。

00:08:11.064 --> 00:08:25.128
Decreasing effort in an exhausted patient can be deterioration, not recovery. Assess air movement, mentation, saturation and carbon dioxide together, and support inadequate breathing promptly.
疲竭患者用力减弱可能是恶化，不是恢复。应综合气流、意识、血氧及二氧化碳，及时支持不足的呼吸。

00:08:25.128 --> 00:08:38.016
Explain the procedure. Select an appropriate limb, avoiding an injury or a known restriction, and support the relaxed arm at heart level. Choose a cuff whose marked size range fits the arm.
解释操作，选择适当肢体，避开受伤或已知受限部位，把放松手臂支撑在心脏水平。选择标注范围适合臂围的袖带。

00:08:38.016 --> 00:08:50.016
Estimate systolic pressure by palpation first, then allow the cuff to deflate before the listening measurement. This guides adequate inflation and helps avoid missing an auscultatory gap.
先触诊估收缩压，放气后再做听诊测量。这样可指导足够充气，并帮助避免漏掉听诊间歇。

00:08:50.016 --> 00:09:04.896
Place the stethoscope over the brachial artery without trapping it under the cuff. Inflate above the estimated systolic value according to the taught method, then deflate steadily, approximately two to three millimetres of mercury per second.
听诊器置于肱动脉上，不压在袖带下。按受训方法充至高于估计收缩压，再以约每秒二到三毫米汞柱平稳放气。

00:09:04.896 --> 00:09:19.872
The first repeated Korotkoff sounds indicate systolic pressure; disappearance usually indicates adult diastolic pressure. If only a palpated systolic value is available, document that method rather than inventing a diastolic.
首次重复 Korotkoff 声对应收缩压，声音消失通常对应成人舒张压。只有触诊收缩压时，应注明方法，不能编造舒张压。

00:09:19.872 --> 00:09:31.128
A cuff that is too small commonly overestimates pressure; an oversized cuff can underestimate it. Use the size markings, not the patient's apparent body type alone.
袖带太小常高估血压，太大可能低估。应看尺寸标识，而不只凭患者外观体型。

00:09:31.128 --> 00:09:41.064
Arm position introduces a hydrostatic effect. A limb well below the heart can produce a higher reading, while a limb above it can produce a lower one.
手臂位置带来静水压影响。明显低于心脏可能读数较高，高于心脏可能较低。

00:09:41.064 --> 00:09:52.464
Movement, shivering, noise, an irregular pulse and rapid cuff deflation can undermine a measurement. Note the limitation and repeat with a better method when feasible.
移动、寒战、噪声、不规则脉搏和过快放气，均可能破坏测量。说明局限，可行时用更好方法复测。

00:09:52.464 --> 00:10:04.536
Do not dismiss a dangerous value as artifact without assessing the patient. A poor signal and genuine shock can coexist; troubleshoot while urgent support and escalation continue.
没有检查患者前，不能把危险值直接归为伪差。信号不好与真实休克可能并存；排错时仍要继续紧急支持和升级处置。

00:10:04.536 --> 00:10:16.656
Systolic pressure is the peak during ventricular contraction; diastolic pressure is the lower pressure between beats. Both depend on several factors, not just how hard the heart squeezes.
收缩压是心室收缩期间峰值；舒张压是两次搏动间较低压力。两者都受多因素影响，不只是心脏收缩力度。

00:10:16.656 --> 00:10:29.976
A systolic pressure around one hundred and twenty with a diastolic around eighty is a familiar example, not every patient's required result. A single acute reading does not diagnose chronic hypertension.
一百二十比八十是熟悉的示例，不是每位患者必须达到的结果。一次急性读数不能诊断慢性高血压。

00:10:29.976 --> 00:10:42.624
A low pressure can suggest poor perfusion, but normal pressure cannot exclude it. Consider mental status, skin, pulse quality, symptoms, bleeding and direction of change.
低血压可提示灌注不良，但正常血压不能排除。应结合意识、皮肤、脉搏质量、症状、出血及变化方向。

00:10:42.624 --> 00:10:52.632
NEWS2 assigns no systolic points between one hundred and eleven and two hundred and nineteen. That score band is not a definition of healthy blood pressure.
NEWS2 在收缩压一百一十一至二百一十九区间不给分。但评分区间不是健康血压的定义。

00:10:52.632 --> 00:11:04.152
For a pressure of one hundred and two over sixty-six, pulse pressure is thirty-six millimetres of mercury. This is subtraction, not the arithmetic mean of the two numbers.
血压一百零二比六十六，脉压为三十六毫米汞柱，是相减，不是两数平均。

00:11:04.152 --> 00:11:20.472
The common MAP approximation adds one third of pulse pressure to diastolic pressure. Here, sixty-six plus twelve gives seventy-eight millimetres of mercury. It is an approximation, especially limited at unusual heart rates or waveforms.
常用平均动脉压近似法，是舒张压加三分之一脉压。本例六十六加十二，得七十八毫米汞柱。这是近似值，极端心率或波形异常时尤其有限。

00:11:20.472 --> 00:11:35.352
Shock index divides heart rate by systolic pressure. One hundred and twelve divided by one hundred and two is about one point one. A raised result can support concern but is modified by age, medication and context.
休克指数是心率除以收缩压。一百一十二除以一百零二约一点一。偏高可支持担忧，但受年龄、药物及背景影响。

00:11:35.352 --> 00:11:45.672
Neither an acceptable MAP estimate nor a shock-index threshold replaces clinical assessment. Do not turn either calculation into a universal fluid prescription.
看似可接受的平均动脉压估计值，或休克指数阈值，都不能代替临床评估，也不能自动变成统一补液处方。

00:11:45.672 --> 00:11:59.616
Mean arterial pressure is the time-averaged pressure over a cardiac cycle. A common teaching approximation is diastolic pressure plus one third of pulse pressure, where pulse pressure is systolic minus diastolic.
平均动脉压是一个心动周期内按时间平均的压力。常用教学近似值为舒张压加三分之一脉压；脉压等于收缩压减舒张压。

00:11:59.616 --> 00:12:14.880
For one hundred and six over sixty-six, pulse pressure is forty. The approximation is sixty-six plus one third of forty, or about seventy-nine millimetres of mercury. Keep the word approximate in the record or explanation.
血压一百零六比六十六，脉压为四十。近似计算为六十六加四十的三分之一，约七十九毫米汞柱。记录或解释时要保留“近似”这一限定。

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:31.728
Oscillometric devices estimate mean pressure from the cuff-oscillation signal and derive systolic and diastolic values with device-specific methods. Check the actual signal, rhythm, cuff and patient context rather than treating a displayed MAP as infallible.
振荡法设备根据袖带振荡信号估计平均压力，并以设备特定方法推导收缩压和舒张压。应检查真实信号、节律、袖带及患者背景，不能把显示的 MAP 当成绝对准确。

00:12:31.728 --> 00:12:50.160
The simple formula is less dependable when heart rate or waveform is unusual. Neither a calculated nor displayed MAP directly proves adequate flow to every tissue; interpret it with perfusion findings, symptoms and serial change, not as an automatic treatment order.
心率或波形异常时，简单公式可靠性较低。计算或显示的 MAP 都不能直接证明所有组织灌流充足；应结合灌注发现、症状及连续变化解释，不能自动变成治疗医嘱。

00:12:50.160 --> 00:13:10.824
Shock Index is heart rate divided by systolic blood pressure. The source measurements have different units; they do not physically cancel. Clinical practice usually reports the index as a number, so retain the actual pulse in beats per minute and pressure in millimetres of mercury. Use credible measurements taken close together.
休克指数等于心率除以收缩压。两个原始测量的单位不同，并不是物理单位相消。临床通常把指数报告为一个数，因此仍应保留实际每分钟心率及毫米汞柱血压。使用时间接近且可信的测量。

00:13:10.824 --> 00:13:23.880
In an original example, ninety-two divided by one hundred and eighteen is about zero point seven eight. Later, one hundred and twenty-eight divided by one hundred and ten is about one point one six.
原创例中，九十二除以一百一十八约为零点七八；之后，一百二十八除以一百一十约为一点一六。

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:46.752
The school gives typical adult examples around zero point five to zero point seven, concern at zero point nine or higher, and higher concern above one. Our rising ratio supports reassessment: pulse rose while systolic pressure fell. These school reference values are not universal diagnostic cutoffs, proof of a cause or an automatic treatment order.
学校给出的成人常见示例约为零点五至零点七，把零点九或以上作为担忧提示，超过一则更值得担忧。本例指数上升支持复评：脉搏加快而收缩压下降。这些学校参考值不是通用诊断界值，不能证明原因，也不自动构成治疗医嘱。

00:13:46.752 --> 00:14:05.976
Pain, fever, pregnancy, age, medicines, rhythm, fitness and measurement error can affect the ratio. Compare it with skin, mentation, bleeding, history and response; do not wait for an unverified cutoff or convert one value into an automatic fluid prescription.
疼痛、发热、妊娠、年龄、药物、节律、体能及测量误差都可能影响指数。要结合皮肤、意识、出血、病史及反应；不能等待未经核实的界值，也不能把一个数值自动换成补液处方。

00:14:05.976 --> 00:14:18.120
Use adequate light and compare with baseline where possible. Describe pallor, mottling and other changes rather than assuming that one skin sign is equally visible in every skin tone.
保证光线，尽可能与基线比较。描述苍白、花斑等变化，不能假设同一体征在所有肤色同样明显。

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:31.656
Feel temperature and moisture. Cool clammy skin can support concern about vasoconstriction and poor perfusion, while early distributive illness can present warm; no single pattern diagnoses the cause.
触查温度和湿度。凉湿皮肤可支持血管收缩及灌注不良担忧，而早期分布性疾病可能皮肤温暖；单一模式不能诊断病因。

00:14:31.656 --> 00:14:46.464
For capillary refill, apply the taught blanching technique, release and time colour return. Approximately two seconds is a common screening reference; document the site, time and conditions rather than only good.
毛细血管再充盈按受训方式压白、松开，并计时颜色恢复。约两秒是常用筛查参考；记录部位、时间及条件，而非只写“好”。

00:14:46.464 --> 00:14:59.520
Cold environment, local vascular disease and measurement technique affect refill. A reassuring refill does not rule out shock, and cyanosis may be absent despite serious hypoxia.
寒冷环境、局部血管病和技术会影响再充盈。再充盈看似正常不能排除休克；严重低氧也可能没有发绀。

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:12.216
Check that the strip matches the meter, is usable and has been stored correctly. Follow local quality-control and manufacturer instructions; a working screen alone does not establish accuracy.
确认试纸匹配仪器、可用且储存正确。遵守当地质控及厂家说明；屏幕亮着不能证明准确。

00:15:12.216 --> 00:15:26.208
Explain the test, prepare a clean dry site and use a single-use lancet on the side of the fingertip. Sugar contamination, wet antiseptic, inadequate sample or excessive squeezing can distort the result.
解释检测，准备清洁干燥部位，以一次性采血针刺指尖侧面。糖污染、未干消毒液、样本不足或过度挤压均会影响结果。

00:15:26.208 --> 00:15:37.704
Apply the sample exactly as the meter requires. The school describes discarding the first drop; the actual device procedure and site preparation determine the approved sampling method.
严格按仪器要求加样。学校描述弃去第一滴，但实际获准采样方式应依据设备规程及部位准备。

00:15:37.704 --> 00:15:49.776
Read and document the unit, usually millimoles per litre here. Dispose of the lancet immediately in the sharps container, and repeat a questionable result using an appropriate reliable method.
读取并记录单位，本地通常为 mmol/L。采血针立即放锐器盒，结果可疑时用适当可靠方法复测。

00:15:49.776 --> 00:16:03.072
Check glucose early with altered consciousness, seizure or unexplained neurological symptoms. Hypoglycemia may resemble intoxication or stroke, and can coexist with another emergency.
意识改变、癫痫或不明神经症状时应尽早查血糖。低血糖可以像醉酒或卒中，也可以与其他急症并存。

00:16:03.072 --> 00:16:19.416
Current BCEHS E01 uses below four millimoles per litre for hypoglycemia. The school flashcard threshold of sixty milligrams per decilitre is not the same number; four millimoles per litre is approximately seventy-two milligrams per decilitre.
现行 BCEHS E01 以低于四 mmol/L 界定低血糖。学校闪卡的六十 mg/dL 不是同一数值；四 mmol/L 约为七十二 mg/dL。

00:16:19.416 --> 00:16:33.552
High glucose with thirst, frequent urination, dehydration or deep breathing suggests a metabolic problem needing assessment. Neither a fruity smell nor a glucose number alone establishes ketoacidosis.
高血糖伴口渴、多尿、脱水或深呼吸，提示需评估代谢问题。水果味气息或单个血糖数字，都不能单独确诊酮症酸中毒。

00:16:33.552 --> 00:16:47.136
After treatment, recheck mental status and glucose and look for recurrence. A corrected number with persistent focal weakness or confusion demands continued investigation, not automatic closure.
治疗后复查意识和血糖并监测复发。数字纠正后仍有局灶无力或混乱，需要继续调查，不能自动结案。

00:16:47.136 --> 00:16:59.856
Apply an appropriate sensor to a suitable site and wait for a stable signal. Compare the displayed pulse with a palpated or otherwise verified rate and inspect the pleth waveform when available.
把适当探头放于适合部位，等待稳定信号。显示脉率应与触诊或其他核实心率比较，有容积波时查看波形。

00:16:59.856 --> 00:17:11.688
Motion, shivering, poor perfusion, cold, nail products and ambient light can interfere. Correct what you can or use another approved site rather than trusting a fluctuating display.
移动、寒战、灌注不良、寒冷、美甲产品及环境光可能干扰。应纠正可纠正因素，或换获准部位，不能相信不断波动的显示。

00:17:11.688 --> 00:17:22.848
Skin pigmentation can affect performance and contribute to missed hypoxemia. Symptoms and other assessment findings still matter when a saturation seems reassuring.
皮肤色素会影响表现，并可能导致漏识别低氧血症。即使血氧读数似乎令人安心，症状及其他评估发现仍很重要。

00:17:22.848 --> 00:17:33.480
Record whether the value was on room air or oxygen, including the delivery device and flow. Do not remove needed oxygen merely to obtain a baseline number.
注明室内空气还是吸氧，包括给氧装置和流量。不要只为取得基线数字而撤去必需氧气。

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:47.712
A saturation near one hundred percent does not measure how much hemoglobin exists, how much blood reaches the tissue or whether ventilation is adequate. Severe anemia or poor perfusion can still compromise oxygen delivery.
饱和度接近百分之百，不测血红蛋白总量、到达组织的血流，也不证明通气足够。严重贫血或灌注不良仍会损害氧输送。

00:17:47.712 --> 00:18:04.416
The school commonly teaches ninety-four to ninety-eight percent, and eighty-eight to ninety-two for chronic respiratory contexts. Current BCEHS A07 has its own general and chronic-hypoxemia targets; those distinctions are taught in the monitoring lesson.
学校常教百分之九十四至九十八，以及慢性呼吸背景下百分之八十八至九十二。现行 BCEHS A07 有自身的一般及慢性低氧目标，监测课会具体区分。

00:18:04.416 --> 00:18:20.760
Oxygen-associated hypercapnia is not explained simply by switching off a hypoxic drive. Gas-distribution changes and hemoglobin carbon-dioxide carriage also matter. Never withhold needed oxygen or ventilation because of that slogan.
氧相关高碳酸血症，不能简单解释为“关掉低氧驱动”。气体分布变化及血红蛋白二氧化碳携带也重要。不能因该口号而不给必要氧气或通气。

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:32.280
A conventional two-wavelength pulse oximeter cannot reliably exclude carbon-monoxide poisoning. Follow exposure-based assessment and care even when ordinary saturation is high.
常规双波长血氧仪不能可靠排除一氧化碳中毒。即使普通血氧高，也应按暴露背景评估照护。

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:43.704
End-tidal carbon dioxide is sampled near the end of expiration. Its value depends on production in tissues, transport by circulation and elimination by ventilation.
呼气末二氧化碳在呼气末段采样，其值依赖组织产生、循环运输以及通气排出。

00:18:43.704 --> 00:18:57.528
When circulation and sampling are adequate, reduced alveolar ventilation tends to increase carbon dioxide. Increased ventilation tends to lower it, but poor perfusion can also lower the exhaled value.
循环及采样足够时，肺泡通气减少倾向使二氧化碳升高，通气增加倾向降低，但灌注不良也会降低呼出值。

00:18:57.528 --> 00:19:11.256
Thirty-five to forty-five millimetres of mercury is a common adult reference. The arterial-to-end-tidal gap can widen with disease, so do not convert an end-tidal number into an assumed arterial result.
三十五至四十五毫米汞柱是常用成人参考。疾病可使动脉与呼气末差值扩大，不能把呼气末数字直接变成假定动脉血气值。

00:19:11.256 --> 00:19:22.224
Look at the waveform as well as the number and patient. A sampling leak, tiny breath or blocked line can change what the instrument reports without showing the true physiology.
同时看波形、数值及患者。漏气、极浅呼吸或采样管堵塞，可能改变显示，而不能代表真实生理。

00:19:22.224 --> 00:19:35.376
A typical time capnogram starts near zero, rises as alveolar gas arrives, develops a plateau and returns toward zero with inspiration. Identify the end-tidal point near the end of the plateau.
典型时间二氧化碳图从接近零开始，肺泡气到达后上升，形成平台，再随吸气回到接近零。呼气末点在平台末端附近。

00:19:35.376 --> 00:19:46.632
A sloping shark-fin appearance suggests obstructed exhalation, but its height can vary. Shape alone neither proves asthma nor dictates a specific medication.
倾斜鲨鱼鳍外观提示呼气受阻，但高度可以不同。单看形状不能确诊哮喘，也不能直接决定某种药物。

00:19:46.632 --> 00:20:01.440
Sudden loss of the waveform requires an immediate patient and equipment check. Consider apnea, airway or circuit disconnection, displaced sampling and severe circulatory change rather than assuming just one cause.
波形突然消失，需要立即检查患者及设备。考虑呼吸暂停、气道或管路断开、采样移位及严重循环变化，而不是只认定一个原因。

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:15.816
During CPR a sustained abrupt rise can suggest improved circulation or ROSC, but confirm clinically at the appropriate check without needless interruption. A single low number does not alone determine termination.
CPR 中持续突然上升可提示循环改善或 ROSC，但应在适当检查时临床确认，避免无必要中断。单个低值也不能独自决定终止复苏。

00:20:15.816 --> 00:20:30.888
The P wave represents atrial depolarization, the QRS ventricular depolarization and the T wave ventricular repolarization. Electrical activation is related to contraction but is not a direct measurement of cardiac output.
P 波代表心房除极，QRS 代表心室除极，T 波代表心室复极。电激活与收缩相关，但不是心输出量的直接测量。

00:20:30.888 --> 00:20:42.096
Prepare the skin, place electrodes correctly and check connections. Movement, poor contact and electrical interference can imitate a dangerous rhythm.
准备皮肤、正确放电极并检查连接。移动、接触不良及电干扰可能模仿危险心律。

00:20:42.096 --> 00:20:51.768
Rate and rhythm monitoring are not equivalent to a diagnostic twelve-lead assessment. A normal-looking single lead cannot rule out myocardial ischemia.
心率节律监测不等于诊断性十二导评估。单导看似正常不能排除心肌缺血。

00:20:51.768 --> 00:21:06.360
ST elevation is interpreted with the appropriate lead pattern, clinical presentation and possible mimics; not every raised segment proves infarction. Detailed acquisition and interpretation return in the school ECG weekend.
ST 抬高需结合相应导联模式、临床表现及可能类似改变；并非每个抬高都证明心肌梗死。详细采集与判读在学校心电周继续学习。

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:19.152
Ventricular fibrillation is chaotic ventricular electrical activity without effective output. Pulseless ventricular tachycardia is also a shockable arrest rhythm under the appropriate protocol.
室颤是无有效输出的混乱心室电活动。无脉室速也属于相应流程中的可除颤骤停心律。

00:21:19.152 --> 00:21:33.744
Asystole is not a shockable rhythm. Verify the tracing and connections without delaying needed CPR. Organized electrical activity without a pulse is pulseless electrical activity, not reassurance.
心静止不是可除颤心律。应核实波形与连接，但不能延误必要 CPR。有组织电活动却无脉是无脉电活动，不是安心信号。

00:21:33.744 --> 00:21:44.760
A wide rapid rhythm with a pulse needs an instability assessment and appropriate clinical support; it is not automatically a command for an unsupervised student to cardiovert.
宽而快的心律若有脉，需要评估不稳定并取得适当临床支持，不是让无督导学生自动做心脏复律的命令。

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:57.120
Possible ischemia requires the full assessment and current pathway. This introduction teaches recognition of danger; it does not replace the allocated resuscitation and ECG modules.
疑似缺血需要完整评估和现行路径。本入门教授识别危险，不能替代学校安排的复苏和心电模块。

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:07.752
Explain the examination and compare both pupils under similar lighting. Record each size in millimetres and whether the shape is round and the sizes equal.
解释检查，在相似照明下比较两侧。分别记录毫米大小、形状是否圆及是否等大。

00:22:07.752 --> 00:22:19.080
Observe constriction of the illuminated pupil and the consensual response in the other eye. Describe reactivity rather than reducing every examination to a normal abbreviation.
观察被照眼瞳孔缩小，以及另一眼的间接反应。描述反应，不要每次都压缩成“正常”缩写。

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:33.096
New unequal pupils with declining consciousness are concerning, but unequal size can also have pre-existing, ocular or medication causes. Pinpoint pupils do not by themselves diagnose opioid poisoning.
新发瞳孔不等大伴意识下降值得担忧，但不等大也可能来自既往状态、眼病或药物。针尖瞳孔本身不能诊断阿片中毒。

00:22:33.096 --> 00:22:42.504
Record a useful baseline and repeat with change. Do not delay urgent airway or circulatory support to complete a detailed light examination.
记录有用基线，有变化时复查。不能为做完整光反射检查而延误紧急气道或循环支持。

00:22:42.504 --> 00:22:57.144
A declining level of consciousness, new weakness or changing pupils needs urgent reassessment. Look for immediately correctable oxygenation, ventilation, perfusion or glucose problems while arranging appropriate support.
意识下降、新发无力或瞳孔变化需要紧急复评。安排适当支持时，同时寻找可立即纠正的氧合、通气、灌注及血糖问题。

00:22:57.144 --> 00:23:11.664
The Cushing pattern combines increased pressure or widened pulse pressure, slow pulse and irregular breathing in a concerning neurological context. It is a late warning, not a screening requirement before concern is justified.
Cushing 模式是在相应神经背景下，血压升高或脉压增宽、脉慢及呼吸不规则的组合。它是晚期警示，不是担忧前必须凑齐的筛查条件。

00:23:11.664 --> 00:23:26.616
A GCS of eight or less signals a high-risk patient, but does not by itself prove traumatic brain injury or select one airway device. Assess airway protection, air movement and available trained resources.
GCS 八分或以下提示高风险，但本身不证明创伤性脑损伤，也不直接选择某个气道器械。应评估气道保护、气流及受训资源。

00:23:26.616 --> 00:23:38.688
A patient with a higher score can still lose airway protection, and a normal score does not exclude serious pathology. Continue source-appropriate neurological and transport assessment.
分数较高者也可能失去气道保护，正常分数也不能排除严重疾病。应继续相应神经评估和转运决策。

00:23:38.688 --> 00:23:50.688
Choose an approved method appropriate to the patient and device. Record route and conditions; oral, tympanic, axillary and true core measurements are not interchangeable.
按患者及设备选择获准方式。记录途径和条件；口腔、鼓膜、腋下及真实核心温度不能互换。

00:23:50.688 --> 00:24:03.600
Fever is commonly defined at thirty-eight degrees Celsius or above, while core temperature below thirty-five is hypothermia. Site, time and the person's baseline influence interpretation.
发热常以三十八摄氏度或以上界定，核心温度低于三十五为低体温。部位、时间及个人基线影响解释。

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:16.968
Heat stroke can include sweating; dry skin is not required. Older or immunocompromised patients can have serious infection without fever, so a normal temperature is not an exclusion test.
热射病可以仍有出汗，不要求皮肤干燥。老年或免疫受损者严重感染可能没有发热，因此正常体温不能用作排除检查。

00:24:16.968 --> 00:24:30.408
Do not infer death or resuscitation stopping from a temperature slogan or an arbitrary rewarming number. Environmental emergencies and resuscitation decisions require their specific current pathway.
不能凭体温口号或任意复温数字判断死亡或停止复苏。环境急症及复苏决策需要专门现行路径。

00:24:30.408 --> 00:24:41.040
Pain is subjective; the patient's report is clinically meaningful. Normal blood pressure, a calm face or a low pulse does not prove that pain is absent.
疼痛主观，患者陈述具有临床意义。血压正常、表情平静或脉搏不快，不能证明没有疼痛。

00:24:41.040 --> 00:25:04.272
Use a zero-to-ten numeric scale when understood, or an appropriate verbal descriptor or faces self-report tool. The school names Wong-Baker FACES. The patient selects the face matching their pain experience; the clinician does not score it by matching the actual facial appearance. Choose an observational tool if reliable self-report is impossible.
理解数字者可用零到十量表，也可用适当言语描述或面部自评工具。学校列出 Wong-Baker FACES。应由患者选择符合自身疼痛体验的面孔，不是医护人员按患者外表情配分。无法可靠自报时，应选择适当观察工具。

00:25:04.272 --> 00:25:19.416
For a person unable to self-report, use an age- and context-appropriate validated observational approach, such as the taught FLACC categories when appropriate: face, legs, activity, cry and consolability.
无法自评者，使用适合年龄和背景的经验证观察法。适当时可用所教 FLACC 项目：面部、腿部、活动、哭声和可安抚性。

00:25:19.416 --> 00:25:34.104
Record the scale, symptom characteristics and functional effect. After an intervention, reassess relief, function and potential adverse effects; a lower score with dangerous sedation is not simple success.
记录量表、症状特征及功能影响。干预后复评缓解、功能及不良反应；分数下降却伴危险镇静，不能简单算成功。

00:25:34.104 --> 00:25:46.896
In this original case, the first pulse pressure is forty-eight and the next is thirty millimetres of mercury. Heart and respiratory rates rise while systolic pressure falls and symptoms worsen.
原创例中，首次脉压四十八，随后三十毫米汞柱。心率和呼吸上升，收缩压下降，症状加重。

00:25:46.896 --> 00:25:58.440
The pattern supports concern for worsening perfusion but does not identify a cause by itself. Check bleeding, illness, chest findings, relevant history and measurement quality.
组合支持灌注恶化担忧，但本身不能确定原因。检查出血、疾病、胸部发现、相关病史及测量质量。

00:25:58.440 --> 00:26:10.080
Do not wait for pressure below ninety before changing urgency. Tell your partner what changed, reassess immediate threats and organize appropriate transport or clinical support.
不要等血压低于九十才改变紧迫程度。告诉同伴发生了什么变化，复评即时威胁，安排适当转运或临床支持。

00:26:10.080 --> 00:26:20.640
Avoid an automatic fluid prescription from the pattern alone. The cause, treatment pathway, contraindications and response determine the authorized intervention.
不能只凭这种模式自动开出补液处方。原因、治疗路径、禁忌及反应，决定获准干预。

00:26:20.640 --> 00:26:34.296
In another original example, deep rapid breathing accompanies thirst, vomiting and high glucose. Low end-tidal carbon dioxide may reflect compensatory ventilation, not merely anxiety.
另一个原创例中，深快呼吸伴口渴、呕吐及高血糖。低呼气末二氧化碳可能反映代偿通气，而非只是焦虑。

00:26:34.296 --> 00:26:50.208
Assess hydration, perfusion, consciousness and possible infection. The combination raises concern for a diabetic metabolic emergency, but requires clinical evaluation rather than a diagnosis from smell or one device.
评估水合、灌注、意识及可能感染。组合提示糖尿病代谢急症担忧，但需要临床评估，不能凭气味或一个设备确诊。

00:26:50.208 --> 00:27:03.888
Do not suppress compensatory breathing by instructing the patient to slow down just to normalize a capnography number. If breathing becomes inadequate, trained support must account for the underlying physiology.
不要只为让二氧化碳数字正常，就要求患者减慢代偿呼吸。若呼吸变得不足，受训支持必须考虑基础生理。

00:27:03.888 --> 00:27:14.136
Document the measured glucose and unit, breathing pattern and serial findings. Continue urgent supportive care and the appropriate conveyance pathway.
记录实际血糖及单位、呼吸模式和连续发现。继续紧急支持照护及相应转运路径。

00:27:14.136 --> 00:27:26.520
A trend requires comparable observations at known times. Changing measurement site, route or oxygen therapy may change the value independently of disease; document those events.
趋势需要已知时间的可比观察。测量部位、途径或给氧改变，都可能独立影响数值，必须记录这些事件。

00:27:26.520 --> 00:27:37.944
Reassess after interventions and movement, and immediately with a new complaint or concern. A fifteen-minute routine interval is not a reason to ignore a sudden change.
干预、搬动后复评，新症状或担忧出现时立即复评。常规十五分钟间隔，不能作为忽略突然变化的理由。

00:27:37.944 --> 00:27:51.240
Improvement must fit the clinical picture. A slower respiratory rate after treatment may be recovery, exhaustion or sedation; check depth, effort, mentation and carbon dioxide.
改善必须与整体情况吻合。治疗后呼吸变慢，可能是恢复、疲竭或镇静，应查深度、呼吸功、意识及二氧化碳。

00:27:51.240 --> 00:28:03.816
Communicate the direction and consequence of change. Saying the pressure fell after movement and the patient is now drowsy is more useful than giving two isolated values with no explanation.
沟通变化方向及后果。“搬动后血压下降，现已嗜睡”比毫无解释地报两个孤立值更有用。

00:28:03.816 --> 00:28:17.280
In supervised practice, demonstrate pulse, respirations, manual pressure, pulse oximetry, glucose preparation and neurological observations. Verbalize why each method is appropriate.
督导练习中示范脉搏、呼吸、手动血压、血氧、血糖准备及神经观察，并说明为何选择这些方式。

00:28:17.280 --> 00:28:28.080
A partner records the actual readings, not a predicted answer. If the instructor supplies a simulated value, label it as simulation rather than a real measurement.
同伴记录真实读数，不写预想答案。教师提供模拟值时，注明模拟，不冒充真实测量。

00:28:28.080 --> 00:28:37.992
Explain one likely source of error and how you would check it. Then integrate the results into a clinical concern rather than reading the numbers back without meaning.
解释一个可能误差来源及核查方法，再把结果综合为临床担忧，而不只是无意义地回报数字。

00:28:37.992 --> 00:28:48.744
Finish with a reassessment after a change and a concise handover. Identify which finding changed urgency and which tempting assumption you deliberately avoided.
最后在情况变化后复评并简短交接。指出什么发现改变了紧迫程度，以及你主动避免了哪个容易出现的假设。
